#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198275 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5793f07d-e0de-5707-a5e1-32d657244e0b" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Intersections of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c00cf5df-4240-5b04-850f-1b4b0d6f8ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c87871c50b343792c73fc18dfe92bc2065b18ed3de1e7bb70324b8b43d027206.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389799} {:answer/id #uuid "1f633a02-8088-56db-88c2-7889ba264321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/39/39db7bc1b259b222a2365441babc3421101961ea26a7143af14b526ba7f81200.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389800} {:answer/id #uuid "6c189e68-bec8-518b-a64d-56fe2a4c4033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ec/ec0e1df36bf5d93b8cdbcc3d14cd510fbe299b929ed3d19f4d901f4461093305.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389801} {:answer/id #uuid "f10813b1-b163-59a5-a38f-0b5b4e7dded5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f90de7c6d88b187af3604912a647620fb88d4833e08fd086cf1a9daae52f331f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389802} {:answer/id #uuid "81b3b685-552f-53ef-8556-c54cf7663b9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/86/8627676ae3b7bcdeff423d79d7289d1d3f9243e0cc69d4f3ac7d3e5c51141fc1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f633a02-8088-56db-88c2-7889ba264321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/39/39db7bc1b259b222a2365441babc3421101961ea26a7143af14b526ba7f81200.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389800} :answer-field/id #uuid "f376ba00-5dab-590e-a791-4441f99a66cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60baa69f-bbf2-5905-831d-ab5e879fa2f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-177648" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,0.5]\\times [0,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,0.5],b\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(0.5,0),$ $(0.5,1),$ and $(0,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5b/5b882f3fb0e7b44eb2df3a510260574e5c4a4d85842a9c0d65515f1a40894756.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times [0,1]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,i],b\\in [0,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(i,0),$ $(i,1),$ and $(0,1).$\n\n![](images/cb/cb530698591dbd71a8058d9faa0c60b636dc654f21e92d65ec8295aeaa67355a.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $\\{0\\}\\times [0,1]:$\n\n![](images/70/704f8f6f0666d09bb2b8a25eab0548c3eb808e2c9d394d2ae873de35cb0112d1.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1204bd88-b470-5b91-b7c2-a8d4ad537898" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/463ae2387423a48dd557af8cfd9b01b6bc08b95f1b3c2f337c6b0c53d3731fa2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389918} {:answer/id #uuid "60caae02-3071-514b-9258-9f96b6664d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389919} {:answer/id #uuid "746ae67c-caa3-593c-9e3f-51831b036f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389920} {:answer/id #uuid "c89a44bf-6d27-578e-9136-6babbb95e931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f28e6f8c8e6e9fa13b5285e25e5460d26548ffd9d71077d1c6073e6c4c743a1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389921} {:answer/id #uuid "51564c2b-bcad-5e6e-9c34-dbd7a16d3a00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/5888cf137eea674995b4c9cc37285b4130df5de3a2a2fa63b1b5b195910526c1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "746ae67c-caa3-593c-9e3f-51831b036f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389920} :answer-field/id #uuid "c241a74d-c7f4-5b96-a451-f6a50f08f04a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bae802a-d591-53eb-b628-21b012d03cee" :question/math-academy-id "q-181968" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={Z}^{-}\\times N$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={Z}^{-}\\times N\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a negative integer and whose $y$-coordinate is a natural number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {Z}^{-},\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/8e/8e6816767cd2010fca1b8991ed9c5e0c42d3a6d6466d78025534bc8362a174b9.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{-2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-2}=\\{(-2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in N\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/4d/4d0fe261e790520e6a8786e6f024d5b9cb7cd54c18242103a1f4b77f09653abc.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-5},{S}_{-4},{S}_{-3}$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…{S}_{-4}\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1} \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in {Z}^{-}}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${Z}^{-}\\times N$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/f7/f7e54dd973126e3179e79b1ba1a26f4a7c1c541ca764b14c4ccef73b4452509e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198806 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198274 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e" :knowledge-point/title "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a224de-0a7a-5ebf-83b7-7575ba7f49c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f8/f8eb09869ae1733a58ed488cc747bca4dddf56ebc0da0de53ff21a2181208217.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284846} {:answer/id #uuid "72e2efff-69aa-52bb-a78c-e682719225d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30c98beaaaf9728a31685195cd236464ceba34094aeda381838f33ba2a134b4c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285846} {:answer/id #uuid "ca095e46-57a5-5045-9532-8b19c4502e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/8210684df0b5143b3b51a3a30cd03e4cdbc4bb80d139c25385dd0fde668d6fd4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286632} {:answer/id #uuid "d08d3be0-ab3c-598f-b81f-c0a937f9bb66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ee/ee6ac65885afc561a40d51352bb6a4eac4974db27274cb35ad3032b7a7a8ffb4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286686} {:answer/id #uuid "efd1c7f0-4319-573c-83f6-fc4b435b4a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c2/c2474d727fe1d97a21f67e9c4ae71b19dcc98106bb7b34c3ccef19ae56b44487.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca095e46-57a5-5045-9532-8b19c4502e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/8210684df0b5143b3b51a3a30cd03e4cdbc4bb80d139c25385dd0fde668d6fd4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286632} :answer-field/id #uuid "39cb9311-07e3-5d93-89a4-7c78cbd6de5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10624e27-fb3c-5852-bfb2-5c112258247b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181984" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the set $S=[-1,1]\\times [0,1]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=[-1,1]\\times [0,1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1],\\,y\\in [0,1]}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [0,1]}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/1c/1cc30fcc7543bfbbf8c5c59d1436eb3b1a0799d60c9ad1d899957e8fd17d58ab.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in [-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [0,1]}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in [-1,1],$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,1).$\n\n![](images/49/494c9d77b0ff339b90792270c9d641054a03a2918e3c56a93747b42a77ee3ccf.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I=[-1,1]:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/7c/7c5ac5dad0aaacb4347c260d634e6bcd2d6102b25d51813fe106803417cc7539.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4" :knowledge-point/title "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13902432-1e15-5d83-9e31-77ea1c9ecb88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a87c5ea8ceaa8a64e30b6375a8bcaa58182ac2e97d68b44c70a0a964c4727dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284963} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc8b5e0-b1db-5812-b923-c8b2aed030ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/340f534cb7548f2e5fcffb6153d45fd327b414aa17247bcde00b5396d24830a4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285222} {:answer/id #uuid "95737d26-61bc-5532-92fe-b8144479975c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/3274c0747b72b6b8ce457f20cd89d0f7d951c8a3bd138c9061448c1bedb42b55.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286146} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d0322b-eee5-55b7-919c-66200da95a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/824d176d4d041be340eb786ff53f8b5a352edca3ad928fc593b9799f2cc4008b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286456} {:answer/id #uuid "ed33c550-8d8c-5c22-8aed-eb90798b7c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b676b2201a4fe4d57cb005eb9527f429068eae4d18c55496ebabf9390fc19219.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13902432-1e15-5d83-9e31-77ea1c9ecb88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9a/9a87c5ea8ceaa8a64e30b6375a8bcaa58182ac2e97d68b44c70a0a964c4727dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284963} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc5ac333-7088-55b5-8dff-47ad3124a244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8eb13b5c-5049-574a-9dd7-f6e99016a3c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-182001" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times [-1,0]$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times [-1,0]\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a integer number and whose $y$-coordinate belongs to $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in [-1,0]}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is in $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}={(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in [-1,0]}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/63/63199d9f35c331339e97ad3b2094a520d1fb6a9892bd0beac83538c43b9e2748.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is in $[-1,0].$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/03/03a6a90b3eff572ceed341de55a0d5e625e338ca18f2ae8ee85eed3bb5278167.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\times N & =…{S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}… \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times [-1,0]$ as the set of vertical lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/9a/9a87c5ea8ceaa8a64e30b6375a8bcaa58182ac2e97d68b44c70a0a964c4727dd.png)"}]}
